WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.894
"Who will be my valentine?" Caroline wondered.

2
00:00:03.895 --> 00:00:09.799
She needed to choose soon—Valentine's Day was the next day!

3
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.562
"Maybe I should choose Tommy," she thought.

4
00:00:13.563 --> 00:00:18.428
"Or perhaps I should choose Tyler!"

5
00:00:18.429 --> 00:00:20.039
"Put your books away.

6
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:24.133
It's time for art," Miss Smith said to the whole class.

7
00:00:24.134 --> 00:00:28.394
"Today we are making Valentine's cards."

8
00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:33.255
"Tommy or Tyler, who will it be," wondered Caroline.

9
00:00:33.256 --> 00:00:40.420
"Maybe if I cut out a big red heart, my heart will help me choose."

10
00:00:40.421 --> 00:00:43.779
Caroline cut out a red paper heart.

11
00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:49.883
When she finished, the heart began to hum. Then,

12
00:00:49.884 --> 00:00:56.449
it jumped up and began to sing, "I am your Valentine's heart. I

13
00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:58.597
am really smart! Write

14
00:00:58.598 --> 00:01:01.793
a poem to the one you love the best. And

15
00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:06.059
I will sing, dance, and do the rest!" Caroline

16
00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.997
wrote her poem. It

17
00:01:07.998 --> 00:01:15.408
was lovely and sweet, but she still didn't know who to give her Valentine's Day heart to. Caroline

18
00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:20.961
added white lace and a small red bow to her heart. Her

19
00:01:20.962 --> 00:01:28.416
heart looked pretty, but still she wondered, "Tommy or Tyler, who should I choose? Who

20
00:01:28.417 --> 00:01:33.218
will receive my Valentine's Day heart?" The

21
00:01:33.219 --> 00:01:37.852
next day was Valentine's Day—February 14! The

22
00:01:37.853 --> 00:01:41.235
classroom was decorated in pink and white. The

23
00:01:41.236 --> 00:01:44.555
children giggled happily. "Now

24
00:01:44.556 --> 00:01:50.345
it is time to give your Valentine's heart away," said Miss Smith. Miss.

25
00:01:50.346 --> 00:01:53.984
Smith had hung a red curtain in the classroom. She

26
00:01:53.985 --> 00:01:56.927
separated the boys and girls. Each

27
00:01:56.928 --> 00:02:00.156
stood on a different side of the curtain. Caroline's

28
00:02:00.157 --> 00:02:05.172
heart beat as she stepped to her side of the curtain. She

29
00:02:05.173 --> 00:02:08.588
still had not chosen her valentine. Then

30
